## 3718. Smallest Missing Multiple of K

## Approach
Store all elements of nums in a HashSet.
Start with the first multiple k.
Keep checking whether the current multiple exists in the set.
If it exists, move to the next multiple by adding k.
Return the first multiple that is missing.

Time: O(n) average
Space: O(n)

SOLUTION :
class Solution {
    public int missingMultiple(int[] nums, int k) {
        HashSet<Integer> set = new HashSet<>();
        for (int i : nums) {
            set.add(i);
        }
        int res = k;
        while (set.contains(res)) {
            res += k;
        }
        return res;
    }
}
